[Chapter "Two Knights (3...Nf6)"]
[Line "Against ...h6"]
[Opening "Italian Game: Two Knights Defense, Modern Bishop's Opening"]

{Black stops Ng5 ideas for good. White carries on with the standard plan.} 1. e4 {Take the centre and open lines for the queen and the f1 bishop.} 1... e5 2. Nf3 {Develop with an attack on e5.} 2... Nc6 3. Bc4 {The Italian: the bishop aims at f7, the weakest square in Black's camp.} 3... Nf6 {Black counterattacks e4.} 4. d3 {Calm and solid: protect e4 and keep the game in Italian structures.} 4... h6 5. c3 {Prepare d4 and a retreat square for the bishop.} 5... d6 6. O-O {Castle; Re1 and a build-up on the queenside come next.} *
